WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.430
<b>Cape Promise</b>

3
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.320
[SANJI]
It's a...

4
00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.530
Flower?

5
00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.260
No it's...

6
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.280
...a person...

7
00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.570
Are ya sure?

8
00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.490
[NAMI]
That old man just
killed a Great King Squid

9
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.120
with one shot!

10
00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.870
[SANJI]
The question is, why...?

11
00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.050
Was he trying to save us?

12
00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:24.960
Or is he just fishing?

13
00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.700
[SANJI]
You gonna say anything?

14
00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.200
Hey, you wanna fight,
we'll fight!

15
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.910
We got cannons back
here, you bastard!

16
00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.290
[CROCUS]
You try it, and someone's
going to die.

17
00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.440
[USOPP, NAMI squeal]

18
00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:11.170
Yeah...? And who's that?

19
00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.380
[CROCUS]
Me, of course.

20
00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.630
'Scuse me?!

21
00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.420
You...!

22
00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.470
Ease up there, bud.

23
00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.890
The old bastard's mocking us!

24
00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:21.180
There's a couple things
we need to know...

25
00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.230
Where are we? And who are you?

26
00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.480
[CROCUS]
You've got some nerve stranger...

27
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:27.940
It's only polite
to introduce yourself

28
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.320
before asking a question
of someone you've just met.

29
00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:35.780
Uh. Heh. All right, fair enough.
I'll go first. My name...

30
00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.660
[CROCUS]
If you must know,

31
00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.440
my name is Crocus,

32
00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.200
and I'm the lighthouse
keeper of the Twin Capes...

33
00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.300
I'm 71-and-a-half years old...

34
00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:43.900
Gemini.

35
00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.070
I'll kill him! I swear it!

36
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.210
[SANJI]
Calm down.

37
00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.370
[CROCUS]
You'd like to know
where we are,

38
00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.070
but your rude behavior
leaves me disinclined

39
00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.880
to accommodate your curiosity,

40
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.470
except that you are trespassing
on my private resort.

41
00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.370
Besides, I'd think
it's pretty obvious,

42
00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.600
seeing as how you were eaten.

43
00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.510
[USOPP]
So you're saying that
we were swallowed by the whale,

44
00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.020
but since when does a whale's
stomach have clouds in it?

45
00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.270
Wait a minute!

46
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.940
If we've been eaten,
what's gonna happen to us?!

47
00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:12.820
I don't wanna be digested!

48
00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.730
[CROCUS]
The exit is over there.

49
00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.240
[CREW]
– We can get out?!
– We can get out?!

50
00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.660
[NAMI]
Okay, even if
I believed a whale's belly

51
00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.260
could have an exit door,

52
00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.950
nothing's there but sky!

53
00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.670
Something's not right here...

54
00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.330
Wait... Look at the sky...

55
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.240
Those seagulls...
Nothing's moving.

56
00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.830
They're painted on!

57
00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.210
It's a giant mural inside
the whale's stomach!

58
00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.420
[NAMI]
Huh?

59
00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.050
[CROCUS]
Call it a doctor's playful mind.

60
00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:39.430
You're not making any sense,
you crazy old fool!

61
00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:41.140
[ZORO]
Easy. Don't let him get to you.

62
00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.220
Yeah, just shut up...

63
00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.410
Nami...

64
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:44.760
If that is an exit,
then we need to get to it...

65
00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.180
Agreed.

66
00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.270
[SANJI]
Aw, great! What now?!

67
00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:54.980
It's begun.

68
00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:56.980
Look!

69
00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.110
That's no island!

70
00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.410
It's some kind of ship!
It's made of iron!

71
00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.740
Yeah, of course!

72
00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.910
'Cause we're floating
on a sea of gastric acid!

73
00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:07.160
[SANJI]
That means a wooden ship
wouldn't fare well

74
00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.580
if it stayed here too long.

75
00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.790
Hey! What's with
this freaky whale?!

76
00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.790
Answer me old man!

77
00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.960
He's very angry.

78
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.690
These aftershocks
are a result of him

79
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.930
hitting his head
against the Red Line.

80
00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.270
What?!

81
00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.340
That explains it...

82
00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.270
Why he had such deep
scars on his forehead.

83
00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.400
Not to mention all
the strange howling...

84
00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.990
Why's he do it?

85
00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.450
[NAMI]
It's because he's suffering!

86
00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.360
[USOPP]
It's all starting to make sense!

87
00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.870
So, what's the geezer up to?

88
00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:52.790
[NAMI]
More than likely he's trying

89
00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.840
to kill the whale
from the inside...

90
00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:56.670
It's time.

91
00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.920
What a despicable
way to kill something.

92
00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.730
Okay, we've solved
the mystery of the whale.

93
00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:01.950
Now how about we find a way out

94
00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.130
of its belly before
it digests us.

95
00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.100
[SANJI]
We have no right
to judge the old man,

96
00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.780
nor do we need
to save the whale.

97
00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:09.480
What we need to
do is focus on how

98
00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.910
to get the hell out of here...

99
00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.430
[USOPP]
We're never gonna get anywhere

100
00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:28.280
if the waves keep
surging like this!

101
00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.410
How can we escape
if we can't even move?!

102
00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.710
[ZORO]
Our only choice is
to paddle! Take the oars!

103
00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:34.060
[NAMI]
Whatever it takes!

104
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.670
We have to find
Luffy right away!

105
00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.040
[ZORO]
I know he's outside!

106
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.000
I caught a glimpse of him
flying out of the whale's mouth!

107
00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.760
[NAMI]
That old guy just jumped in!

108
00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:44.550
Huh?

109
00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.140
[ZORO]
Is he insane?

110
00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.550
The acid will eat him alive.

111
00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:59.430
Aaaah!

112
00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.950
So dizzy! I'm gonna hurl.

113
00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.200
[LUFFY]
Hey, that's weird...

114
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.000
The whale's got
a river inside it, too?

115
00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.700
[MR. 9]
Things are looking up, my dear!

116
00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.770
We've been successful so far.

117
00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.850
Listen carefully,
Miss Wednesday...

118
00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.390
<b>Miss Wednesday
Mysterious Woman</b>

119
00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.620
Behind these doors
lie the beast's stomach,

120
00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:37.270
and that troublesome
geezer as well.

121
00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:39.900
He must be eliminated
before he can interfere again.

122
00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.780
<b>Mr. 9
Mysterious Man</b>

123
00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.780
Remember... it's all
for the whale.

124
00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.780
Indeed, Mr. 9...

125
00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.640
This whale's
a precious creature,

126
00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:49.240
and one that holds the sweet
promise of life for our town.

127
00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.080
Guys! Crocus just resurfaced!

128
00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:55.080
[ZORO]
Look, forget about the old guy!

129
00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.580
Our focus should be on finding
a way to open these doors.

130
00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.590
All right...

131
00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.090
Here's the plan baby.
"Three... Two... One..."

132
00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:05.210
Then we kick through the doors.

133
00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.930
Roger that, Mr. 9.

134
00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.180
I'm ready any time.

135
00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:11.710
[distant scream growing louder]

136
00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.470
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
What is that voice, Mr. 9?

137
00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.440
[MR. 9]
I don't know, Miss Wednesday.

138
00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.510
[LUFFY]
I can't stop!

139
00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.190
They're back...

140
00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:34.010
[MR. 9]
Not good! We're
gonna fall into gastric acid!

141
00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:36.060
[ZORO]
Luffy?

142
00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.160
[LUFFY]
Zoro! Is everyone okay?

143
00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.620
So, um... I could use a hand!

144
00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:48.180
Looks like Luffy's not alone...

145
00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.910
Who do you suppose the
two weirdoes are with him?

146
00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.030
[NAMI]
Where'd that old geezer
disappear to?!

147
00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.270
[ZORO]
Forget him...
We need to save Luffy!

148
00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:12.190
[CROCUS]
You've got to stop it, Laboon.

149
00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.620
You can't afford to beat
yourself up any more...

150
00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.960
There's only a tiny
amount of sedative left.

151
00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:21.910
And until I can make some
more you'll have to make nice.

152
00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:24.760
I've told you before...

153
00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.300
that wall divides
the world's oceans.

154
00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.860
It doesn't matter how
many times you hit it...

155
00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:30.760
It won't break.

156
00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.300
Not even for someone
as mighty as you.

157
00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.600
[NAMI]
I don't claim to speak whale,

158
00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.350
but it seems to
have calmed down a bit.

159
00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.230
[ZORO]
Seems that way.

160
00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.780
[ZORO]
Now, we saved your lives
for the time being,

161
00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.320
but you'd better talk
and make it quick!

162
00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:52.110
Mr. 9, these
heathens are pirates!

163
00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.280
Yes, that's painfully
obvious, Miss Wednesday.

164
00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.980
But, if we speak to their
humanity and compassion,

165
00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:59.790
they should understand our
plight... Maybe.

166
00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.250
[CROCUS]
You parasites are still here?!

167
00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.170
I grow weary of this,
and for the last time!

168
00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.300
As long as I draw breath,

169
00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.340
you will not lay a single,
harmful finger on Laboon!

170
00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.140
He's back again.

171
00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.380
[LUFFY]
Who's the old guy?

172
00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:17.720
[MISS WEDNESDAY laughs]

173
00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.680
You can't bully us into
abandoning our mission.

174
00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.030
[MR. 9]
We were sent
here to hunt this whale,

175
00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.390
and that's exactly
what we're going to do!

176
00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:26.270
And this time,
we won't let you interfere!

177
00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:29.320
We're about to give
this whale a new blowhole!

178
00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.510
Fire, baby!

179
00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.000
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
Roger!

180
00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.420
He jumped straight
into the line of fire!

181
00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.920
Did he just... Was he
protecting the whale?!

182
00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:52.880
[MR. 9]
Go ahead... Waste your time!

183
00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.990
But, make no mistake...

184
00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:59.220
That hulking beast will
provide food for our town!

185
00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:05.030
[MR. 9, MISS WEDNESDAY laugh]

186
00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.360
What's going on?

187
00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:15.650
[USOPP]
Um... What was that for?

188
00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:16.910
I just... wanted to hit 'em.

189
00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.150
[CROCUS]
I thank you for saving my life,

190
00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:24.250
though I must ask...

191
00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.580
Why did you do it?

192
00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.170
[LUFFY]
I wasn't trying to save you...

193
00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.460
There was just something
about those two I didn't like.

194
00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:30.770
[CROCUS]
Oh...

195
00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:32.570
[NAMI]
Okay, I think it's
time we got some answers.

196
00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.380
Who are these guys?

197
00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.760
And how did you
end up inside this whale?

198
00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:38.860
[CROCUS]
These two are
thugs from a nearby town,

199
00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:39.960
looking for whale meat...

200
00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.770
If they caught him, Laboon
could feed the townspeople

201
00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:45.170
for at least 2 or 3 years, easy.

202
00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:46.370
All they're concerned with

203
00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:49.040
is filling their
fat, greedy bellies!

204
00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:49.810
Laboon?

205
00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.900
That's the whale's name.

206
00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.910
He's a unique and
magnificent creature...

207
00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:57.240
An island whale one of the
largest species in the world

208
00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:59.990
that can only be found
in the West Blue...

209
00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:03.120
I won't allow them to
slaughter him for food.

210
00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.750
It's a shame that
he's stuck here

211
00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.920
so far away from his domain...

212
00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.270
You see, there's a reason
he keeps hitting himself

213
00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.090
on the Red Line and
howling at Reverse Mountain.

214
00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:12.840
[NAMI]
There is?

215
00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.050
Yes... To put it one way...

216
00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:19.970
Inside Laboon's body
beats the heart of a human...

217
00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:22.890
He has most impatiently awaited

218
00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.390
and is eternally devoted to
a certain band of pirates...

219
00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.270
[CROCUS]
Going on 50 long years now.

220
00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.810
[CROCUS]
Listen closely,

221
00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.240
and I will reveal to you
Laboon's tragic story.

222
00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.530
[CROCUS]
One fine sunny day,

223
00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:54.420
while I was fulfilling my duties
as the lighthouse keeper,

224
00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:58.800
some good-natured pirates
came down Reverse Mountain.

225
00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:03.440
They were followed by a
baby whale, spry and chipper,

226
00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:08.680
whom I would soon come to know
as the one and only, Laboon.

227
00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:13.730
[CROCUS]
He is an Island Whale,
one of the largest in the world.

228
00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.400
They are a rare species
found only in the West Blue.

229
00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.670
Laboon had developed
a bond with the pirates,

230
00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:20.400
traveling with them
for much of their journey.

231
00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.920
But knowing the dangers
of the Grand Line,

232
00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:27.120
the pirates chose to leave
Laboon behind in the West Blue.

233
00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.540
[CROCUS]
But the stubborn little
whale followed them anyway.

234
00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.920
As a general rule, Island
Whales are social animals,

235
00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.590
and travel together
in family groups.

236
00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:38.700
I suspect that Laboon
had somehow come to feel

237
00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:41.050
that those pirates
were his family.

238
00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.740
The wear and tear on the
pirates' ship was quite severe,

239
00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.390
so they stayed here
for several months.

240
00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:48.440
In that time, I, too, was able

241
00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.140
to forge a close
relationship with them.

242
00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.730
Thus, when the day of their
departure finally arrived.

243
00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.360
[CAPTAIN]
I have a favor to ask
of you, my dear friend.

244
00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.990
Could you look after
Laboon for a few years?

245
00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:02.340
When my men and I have completed

246
00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.070
our voyage around the world,
we'll be back.

247
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:07.870
[CAPTAIN]
Listen to me, Laboon...

248
00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:11.460
We're taking our ship to
the end of the Grand Line.

249
00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:13.870
Until we return, I need you
to wait for us here with Crocus.

250
00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:16.130
You can't come with us...

251
00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:18.460
It's too dangerous, even
for a mighty whale like you.

252
00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:21.920
Don't worry three years
will pass by like a flash.

253
00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.180
And don't forget...

254
00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:26.430
No matter the distance,
our friendship lasts forever.

255
00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.390
Well, I guess it's time!

256
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.980
[CAPTAIN]
All right, men!

257
00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.610
We're setting sail!
Hoist the anchor!

258
00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.190
[CREW cheers]

259
00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:46.700
[CROCUS]
Laboon!

260
00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:49.990
You have to wait for us here
and mind Crocus, Laboon.

261
00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.450
Don't worry we'll be back...

262
00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.080
I promise.

263
00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:09.560
[CROCUS]
That was fifty long years ago.

264
00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:10.810
[SANJI]
Fifty years?!

265
00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:12.920
So, Laboon has been
waiting all this time

266
00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.180
for his friends to return...

267
00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.940
No wonder he's upset...

268
00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:18.230
That kind of wait
would drive anyone crazy!

269
00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:30.200
[ZORO]
This is some canal...

270
00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.480
Amazing this
whale's still alive,

271
00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.250
with a hole like
this in his body.

272
00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.870
[SANJI]
I suppose you're
responsible for this?

273
00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.710
[CROCUS]
Just a doctor's playful mind...

274
00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:37.580
[USOPP]
Doctor?!

275
00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:38.480
That's right.

276
00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.840
Legally certified...

277
00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:43.090
I also ran a clinic on
the cape once upon a time.

278
00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:45.720
Before that, I served
as a ship's doctor.

279
00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:46.930
[LUFFY]
Really?

280
00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:47.800
That's great...

281
00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.510
Then join us,
we need a doctor.

282
00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.310
[CROCUS]
Don't be ridiculous.

283
00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.820
I no longer have
that kind of energy.

284
00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.480
Exploring the seas is
a young man's burden.

285
00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.890
[SANJI]
What kind of a doctor
hollows out

286
00:15:57.920 --> 00:15:58.770
the inside of a whale...

287
00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.480
[NAMI]
Maybe it's part of
the treatment.

288
00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.480
The girl is right...

289
00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:03.560
With a creature of this size,

290
00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.370
it's virtually impossible to
treat it from the outside.

291
00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:09.020
Therefore, I devised a more
drastic solution.

292
00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:10.590
Here's the exit...

293
00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:25.380
[LUFFY]
The sky.

294
00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:36.060
What is it?

295
00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.480
[USOPP]
Don't you think
fifty years is a bit extreme?

296
00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:42.940
Those pirates sure know how
to test someone's patience!

297
00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.190
[SANJI]
Idiot! Don't ya get it?

298
00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:46.280
This is the Grand Line.

299
00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.030
His friends are dead.

300
00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.030
Ugh! Why are you all
being so pessimistic?

301
00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.260
You don't know
that they're dead!

302
00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:56.290
They could still
come back for him!

303
00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:58.350
Come on. Have some
sympathy, will ya?!

304
00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.120
I thought it was very touching!

305
00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.340
I mean a whale still
believing a promise

306
00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.340
his friends made
despite all these years?!

307
00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:05.460
That's a true bond!
Right, pops?!

308
00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.800
[CROCUS]
Indeed...

309
00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:10.050
But the lesson here
is that reality is cruel.

310
00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:12.080
Laboon's cohorts aren't dead.

311
00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:14.680
The truth is, they
abandoned their quest.

312
00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.770
I learned that they turned tail
and left the Grand Line.

313
00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.310
[USOPP]
I don't believe it.

314
00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.230
I mean, why abandon
him like that?

315
00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.570
[NAMI]
You say they ran
away from the Grand Line.

316
00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:27.940
Do you know if they made it
through the Calm Belt alive?

317
00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.400
[CROCUS]
I can't claim to know
exactly what became of them,

318
00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.860
but I doubt they'll ever
come back here again.

319
00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:37.810
Seasons, weather, currents, wind
direction... on the Grand Line,

320
00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.430
these elements seem to
defy the very laws of nature.

321
00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:43.260
Common sense is useless,

322
00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:46.700
and the terror of that fact
can be quite overwhelming.

323
00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:48.690
So, if I've got this straight,
what you're saying is,

324
00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.170
these pirates were
a bunch of cowards,

325
00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.360
who cared more about
saving their own asses,

326
00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:54.050
than keeping a
promise to a friend?

327
00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:58.600
Why would anyone abandon
such a loyal creature?!

328
00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.350
Just look at him!

329
00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.230
It's cruelty on a grand scale!

330
00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:04.500
But if you've known all this,
why haven't you told him?

331
00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:07.570
Laboon can obviously
communicate with you.

332
00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.260
He seems to understand
humans quite well for a whale.

333
00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:11.390
[CROCUS]
I did tell him...

334
00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:13.490
...down to the last,
miserable detail.

335
00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.280
I know this isn't what you want
to hear, but it's the truth.

336
00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:19.330
Your friends left
the Grand Line.

337
00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.210
The bond you shared
with each other was real.

338
00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:26.210
Just as real as the promise they
made to return for you one day.

339
00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.090
[CROCUS]
But, still... face the facts...

340
00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:36.600
Those men are
never coming back.

341
00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:42.710
[LABOON roars mournfully]

342
00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:59.530
Laboon! Please!

343
00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.240
I say this for your own good!
They're not coming back!

344
00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:13.010
I understand that
you don't wanna accept it!

345
00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:17.140
But you need to realize
that this is how things are!

346
00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.110
Listen...

347
00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.600
Laboon!

348
00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.940
[CROCUS]
That was the day
that Laboon began

349
00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:40.700
to howl at Reverse Mountain...

350
00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.330
Soon after, he started slamming
his body against the Red Line.

351
00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.250
It's as if he believes that wall
is what keeps his friends away,

352
00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:51.000
and by breaking it, he can
clear the path for their return.

353
00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:52.880
[SANJI]
I admire his dedication...

354
00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:55.050
[USOPP]
Never gave up on 'em.

355
00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:56.510
He refuses to believe me,

356
00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.240
because then he'd have
to admit that it's over.

357
00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:01.770
And that terrifies him
more than anything.

358
00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:04.170
There's no way for him to
go back to the West Blue...

359
00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:08.640
So, what we have is a
paradox of tragic proportions.

360
00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:12.380
Laboon is a lost soul dying
to live with his friends,

361
00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.480
but won't stop killing
himself to reach them...

362
00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:18.490
Tragedy. Still for all the grief
those pirates put him through

363
00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:21.280
they did the same to you by
saddling you with their burden.

364
00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:25.740
I mean you've done
enough for Laboon.

365
00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:26.590
What about you...?

366
00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.640
[CROCUS]
The scars on his hide are deep.

367
00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.020
Those in his heart
are even deeper...

368
00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:32.900
He needs someone
to tend his wounds,

369
00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.300
and I'm all he's got...

370
00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:37.560
For years, he's battered himself
while I've patched him up...

371
00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:40.100
A strange friendship,
but it works.

372
00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.140
What the hell
is that idiot up to?

373
00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:45.890
Ya gotta watch
him every second...

374
00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:47.850
[SANJI]
We've been watching him,
look what happens...

375
00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:52.270
[LUFFY]
Gum-Gum...

376
00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.360
...Flower Arrangement!

377
00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.490
Think he's aware
that's our mast...?

378
00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:58.490
And now it's on top of a whale.

379
00:20:58.490 --> 00:20:59.780
Why'd he do that?

380
00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.410
Hey Luffy, stop
tearing up the ship.

381
00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:09.380
[howls]

382
00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:12.290
You... ass...! Luffy... stop...!

383
00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:23.550
The boy...! He's dead!

384
00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:24.800
Oh don't worry...!

385
00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.970
It'll take way more
than that to kill Luffy!

386
00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:32.600
Ha...! Gotcha!

387
00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.780
What does he
think he's doing?!

388
00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:46.500
[ZORO]
You wanna let us in on your plan

389
00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:47.990
before ya kill yourself?!

390
00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:53.960
[LUFFY]
It's a draw!

391
00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:00.050
[LUFFY]
I'm stronger than I look!

392
00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:04.550
I can always tell when
someone's itching to fight...

393
00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.560
Well, if you want a battle,
I'll gladly give you one...

394
00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:10.140
Your shipmates used to
spar with you, didn't they?

395
00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.280
You miss it.

396
00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:14.270
Well, I can rival
anything they threw at ya!

397
00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:15.180
Tell ya what...

398
00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:17.050
after me and my friends
travel the Grand Line,

399
00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:18.880
we'll come back
here and find you.

400
00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:25.660
And then you better be
ready for a rematch!

401
00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:38.210
[LUFFY]
Hey, not bad!

402
00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:40.210
Consider this a
symbol of my promise

403
00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:42.090
to come do battle with you...

404
00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:43.600
Of course, it's a
rush paint job,

405
00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:46.050
so you'll have to be careful
and avoid hitting your head

406
00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:47.050
or you'll rub it right off.

407
00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:48.100
Understand?

408
00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:53.270
Good whale!

409
00:22:55.150 --> 00:22:56.270
[USOPP]
Where are they?

410
00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:59.610
Where are who...?
Oh, you mean those two weirdoes?

411
00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:01.110
I guess they escaped.

412
00:23:01.110 --> 00:23:03.300
Must have happened when
we were distracted by Laboon.

413
00:23:03.300 --> 00:23:04.400
I wonder who they were...

414
00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:08.850
Miss Wednesday...

415
00:23:08.850 --> 00:23:10.620
What are we going to do now?

416
00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:13.940
First, put some
distance between us

417
00:23:13.970 --> 00:23:14.600
and these morons.

418
00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:16.610
Then we report to the Boss.

419
00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:19.420
Our time for completing this
mission has long since run out.

420
00:23:19.420 --> 00:23:21.000
[MR. 9]
I can hear the others now.

421
00:23:21.150 --> 00:23:23.380
They're probably
already calling us traitors.

422
00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:24.510
I know...

423
00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:25.340
But without our weapons,

424
00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.840
we've no choice but to go back
to the office and start over.

425
00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:31.970
[MR. 9]
And this time no
one will stop us...

426
00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:33.100
Aaaah!

427
00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:34.310
No, no! I couldn't have!

428
00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:35.640
What is it?

429
00:23:37.190 --> 00:23:37.900
It's... gone.

430
00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:38.520
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
What?!

431
00:23:39.070 --> 00:23:40.380
[LUFFY]
Huh?

432
00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:42.190
Hmm... What's this thing?

433
00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:44.990
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
How could you have
lost the Log Pose?!

434
00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:46.160
[MR. 9]
I don't know!

435
00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:48.320
I must've dropped it somewhere!

436
00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:50.900
But we're not going
anywhere without it...

437
00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:52.120
- [MISS WEDNESDAY] How awful!
- [MR. 9 gasps]

438
00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:56.000
Ah! No! This can't
be happening...

439
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:56.710
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
Wha...?!

440
00:23:58.290 --> 00:23:59.540
[MR. 9]
It's...! Ahhhh...

441
00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:02.460
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
Oh no!

442
00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:04.670
[MR. 9]
The Unluckies!

443
00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:05.970
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
We're out of time!

444
00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:08.890
<b>Miss Friday

Mysterious
Vulture Mr. 13

Mysterious
Sea Otter</b>

445
00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:07.050
[MR. 9]
Mr. 13!

446
00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:08.890
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
Miss Friday!

447
00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:09.720
Don't be hasty!

448
00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:11.550
Please, we can explain!

449
00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:13.830
We'll check in with
Boss immediately!

450
00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:15.090
Aaaah!

451
00:24:18.110 --> 00:24:20.040
[screams]

452
00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:29.910
Okay, then!

453
00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:31.040
I finally have some
peace and quiet

454
00:24:31.040 --> 00:24:32.740
so I can work on a plan
for the Grand Line journey.

455
00:24:37.540 --> 00:24:41.420
Ah... Don't think I forgot about
you, Elephant Blue Fin Tuna!

456
00:24:41.420 --> 00:24:42.920
Damn... That's my life...!

457
00:24:43.880 --> 00:24:47.880
Luffy breaks it then
I put it back together!

458
00:24:47.880 --> 00:24:49.180
Hey, get off your lazy butt
and give me a hand!

459
00:24:49.180 --> 00:24:51.970
This ship isn't gonna
fix itself you know!

460
00:24:52.140 --> 00:24:56.380
[NAMI screams]

461
00:24:57.890 --> 00:24:59.480
You mind? Keep it down.

462
00:24:59.480 --> 00:25:01.350
[SANJI]
Is there some problem,
my dearest Nami?!

463
00:25:01.350 --> 00:25:03.520
If it's food you're worried
about, say no more!

464
00:25:03.520 --> 00:25:04.320
[USOPP]
Someone say "food"?

465
00:25:04.650 --> 00:25:06.780
You idiots!
The compass is broken!

466
00:25:07.400 --> 00:25:08.990
The needle just spins!
It won't stop!

467
00:25:08.990 --> 00:25:10.660
Oh, yeah, you're right.

468
00:25:10.660 --> 00:25:12.780
I don't know about you,
but I'm getting dizzy!

469
00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:14.450
Whoa... This is cool!

470
00:25:15.330 --> 00:25:17.150
It is sadly apparent
that none of you

471
00:25:17.220 --> 00:25:19.250
possess the slightest knowledge
about how things work here...

472
00:25:19.250 --> 00:25:22.330
Did you all come here to die?

473
00:25:22.790 --> 00:25:24.130
Ah, great spread!

474
00:25:24.130 --> 00:25:25.960
It's for everyone!

475
00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:27.420
[CROCUS]
There is nothing
wrong with your compass.

476
00:25:27.420 --> 00:25:30.840
The Grand Line has little
regard for the rules of the sea.

477
00:25:30.840 --> 00:25:34.140
Common sense is
useless in this place.

478
00:25:34.930 --> 00:25:37.140
The needle... Why does it spin?

479
00:25:37.140 --> 00:25:38.220
[CROCUS]
Because we are surrounded

480
00:25:38.220 --> 00:25:40.420
by a powerful magnetic field.

481
00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:43.610
The islands here are riddled
with magnetic minerals,

482
00:25:43.610 --> 00:25:46.360
which cause all
sorts of abnormalities.

483
00:25:46.380 --> 00:25:49.090
Also, the winds and
currents lack constancy

484
00:25:49.150 --> 00:25:50.320
in their patterns.

485
00:25:50.490 --> 00:25:54.140
As a navigator, I'm sure you
can appreciate this dilemma.

486
00:25:54.140 --> 00:25:54.980
So then...

487
00:25:55.010 --> 00:25:56.580
If we don't have
a way to tell direction,

488
00:25:56.610 --> 00:25:57.830
this whole trip is hopeless...

489
00:25:57.830 --> 00:25:58.790
Yummy!

490
00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:00.060
I don't know what to say...

491
00:26:00.140 --> 00:26:01.000
We're screwed...

492
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.540
Hey! You're the navigator,
so navigate us outta here!

493
00:26:03.540 --> 00:26:06.000
This is delicious!
You oughta try some!

494
00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:07.750
Would all of you just
shut up for five seconds

495
00:26:07.780 --> 00:26:08.960
so I can figure this out!

496
00:26:08.990 --> 00:26:11.860
This nose of the Elephant
Tuna is my favorite part!

497
00:26:11.860 --> 00:26:12.900
Tasty!

498
00:26:12.930 --> 00:26:15.030
If you have any hope of
navigating the Grand Line,

499
00:26:15.510 --> 00:26:17.600
you're going to need
a Log Pose to guide you.

500
00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:18.640
[NAMI]
Log Pose?

501
00:26:18.640 --> 00:26:19.850
I've never heard of it.

502
00:26:19.850 --> 00:26:20.980
It's a specially
designed compass

503
00:26:21.290 --> 00:26:23.850
that can record levels
of magnetism.

504
00:26:23.850 --> 00:26:25.400
[LUFFY]
Is it strange looking?

505
00:26:25.400 --> 00:26:27.980
Why, yes, it does
have an odd shape.

506
00:26:27.980 --> 00:26:29.400
[LUFFY]
Something like this?

507
00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:30.530
Yes, exactly...

508
00:26:30.990 --> 00:26:33.540
Only a fool courting
disaster would attempt

509
00:26:33.570 --> 00:26:35.910
to travel the
Grand Line without one.

510
00:26:36.660 --> 00:26:38.160
Understood...

511
00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:39.910
Excuse me for one second.

512
00:26:40.410 --> 00:26:41.830
So...

513
00:26:42.210 --> 00:26:44.830
Why didn't you tell me you
had one of those Log things?!

514
00:26:46.540 --> 00:26:48.150
[LUFFY]
I found it on deck,
just laying there.

515
00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.630
Those two weirdoes must've
dropped it when they escaped.

516
00:26:50.630 --> 00:26:51.800
Did they?

517
00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:53.170
[LUFFY]
Why'd you hit me?

518
00:26:53.170 --> 00:26:54.130
Felt like it...

519
00:26:54.130 --> 00:26:55.090
[LUFFY]
Oh, okay.

520
00:26:56.340 --> 00:26:59.220
Huh, but there isn't a
dial face on this thing.

521
00:26:59.220 --> 00:27:01.880
[CROCUS]
You don't need one.
It's a special brand

522
00:27:01.910 --> 00:27:04.250
of magnetism that runs
through the Grand Line islands.

523
00:27:04.530 --> 00:27:06.810
Complete with its own set of
rules that makes it possible

524
00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:08.700
to get around.

525
00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:11.990
By recording the level of
magnetism between two islands,

526
00:27:11.990 --> 00:27:14.490
you can chart a route
from one island to the next.

527
00:27:15.160 --> 00:27:18.060
The log pose method
is really the only choice.

528
00:27:18.130 --> 00:27:20.500
Since the magnetism here
presents huge problems

529
00:27:20.660 --> 00:27:22.630
for conventional navigation...

530
00:27:22.630 --> 00:27:25.980
As it turns out Reverse Mountain
is a great starting point.

531
00:27:25.980 --> 00:27:29.130
It produces seven
levels of magnetism.

532
00:27:29.130 --> 00:27:32.050
But it doesn't matter which one
you choose to start with.

533
00:27:32.050 --> 00:27:34.280
Eventually all of them
will pull against each other

534
00:27:34.320 --> 00:27:35.930
and form one route.

535
00:27:35.930 --> 00:27:39.470
And the island at the
end of that route...

536
00:27:39.970 --> 00:27:41.310
...is Raftel.

537
00:27:41.310 --> 00:27:44.100
The last and most mysterious
in the Grand Line...

538
00:27:44.100 --> 00:27:44.960
Its very existence
was confirmed

539
00:27:44.960 --> 00:27:47.890
by the King of the Pirates,
the only known person

540
00:27:47.960 --> 00:27:50.440
to have traveled the
Grand Line in its entirety.

541
00:27:50.440 --> 00:27:51.820
Raftel...

542
00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:52.890
That's it!

543
00:27:52.890 --> 00:27:54.730
That must be where
the One Piece is hidden...

544
00:27:54.910 --> 00:27:56.580
[CROCUS]
That's the most
prominent theory,

545
00:27:57.700 --> 00:28:00.410
but no one's been able to
set foot on Raftel Island since.

546
00:28:00.410 --> 00:28:03.580
Don't worry.
We'll know soon enough!

547
00:28:06.460 --> 00:28:07.700
Well, I'm satisfied!

548
00:28:07.700 --> 00:28:09.170
You guys ready to go?

549
00:28:09.170 --> 00:28:11.000
I told you that
was for all of us!

550
00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:12.670
He... He even ate the bones!

551
00:28:12.670 --> 00:28:13.470
A Log Pose...

552
00:28:14.180 --> 00:28:15.970
We have to take
special care of this...

553
00:28:15.970 --> 00:28:18.180
It's the key to finding the
greatest treasure of all time!

554
00:28:18.180 --> 00:28:19.930
You greedy, bottomless pit!

555
00:28:19.930 --> 00:28:22.560
You ate the meal
I made for Nami!

556
00:28:23.350 --> 00:28:26.480
Well I hope you left room...
for your dessert!

557
00:28:41.370 --> 00:28:42.330
[LUFFY]
Ow! Why's everyone hitting me?!

558
00:28:42.420 --> 00:28:44.050
[SANJI]
You never think of
anyone but yourself and...!

559
00:28:44.050 --> 00:28:44.550
[NAMI]
Sanji...

560
00:28:44.740 --> 00:28:46.200
[SANJI]
Yes...?

561
00:28:47.280 --> 00:28:48.780
[NAMI]
Both of you get out of my sight

562
00:28:48.860 --> 00:28:55.400
before I wring your necks!

563
00:28:55.430 --> 00:28:56.700
[USOPP]
Okay, so...

564
00:28:57.010 --> 00:28:57.940
Correct me if I'm wrong,

565
00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:00.300
but doesn't the Log Pose work
better when it's not broken?!

566
00:29:00.300 --> 00:29:02.800
Oh no... Our log pose is ruined!

567
00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:04.160
[CROCUS]
Calm yourselves...

568
00:29:04.160 --> 00:29:05.140
I will give you my own...

569
00:29:05.560 --> 00:29:08.060
...as a "thank you"
for helping Laboon.

570
00:29:15.570 --> 00:29:17.570
Oh good, I'm not dead...

571
00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:21.670
[SANJI]
Hello, dear lady.

572
00:29:21.780 --> 00:29:23.320
Allow me to
help you to your feet.

573
00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:24.370
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
Oh, thank you.

574
00:29:24.370 --> 00:29:25.580
[SANJI]
Nice day, don't you think?

575
00:29:25.580 --> 00:29:26.370
[MR. 9]
Hey!

576
00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:28.290
We need a favor.

577
00:29:31.920 --> 00:29:33.210
[LUFFY]
Whisky Peak?

578
00:29:33.540 --> 00:29:34.750
Huh. That's a funny name.

579
00:29:34.750 --> 00:29:35.840
[USOPP]
So what is it?

580
00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:38.590
[MR. 9]
That's where we live... Um, sir.

581
00:29:38.590 --> 00:29:39.470
[NAMI]
How were you stranded?

582
00:29:39.700 --> 00:29:40.720
Where's your ship?

583
00:29:40.720 --> 00:29:43.180
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
Well... It was destroyed.

584
00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:46.340
Asking us for a
ride is pushing it, Mr. 9;

585
00:29:46.340 --> 00:29:47.890
especially after you
tried to kill the whale?

586
00:29:48.310 --> 00:29:49.300
What's with the wardrobe?

587
00:29:49.300 --> 00:29:50.230
What are you supposed to be?

588
00:29:50.230 --> 00:29:51.940
I am a king!

589
00:29:52.940 --> 00:29:53.760
You're lying.

590
00:29:53.760 --> 00:29:54.930
No, please!

591
00:29:55.390 --> 00:29:56.490
We can't say!

592
00:29:56.570 --> 00:29:57.770
She's right.

593
00:29:57.860 --> 00:30:00.190
You have to believe us, our only
motive here is getting home.

594
00:30:00.260 --> 00:30:02.630
We'd tell you everything
if we could, it's just that...

595
00:30:02.630 --> 00:30:04.670
..."mystery" is
our company's motto.

596
00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:06.460
You see, we have
to be mysterious!

597
00:30:06.460 --> 00:30:07.600
It's sort of a rule...

598
00:30:07.740 --> 00:30:09.350
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
We have confidence
in your character.

599
00:30:09.400 --> 00:30:11.120
Can't you give us
the same courtesy?!

600
00:30:11.260 --> 00:30:12.430
[MR. 9]
Please! We're begging you!

601
00:30:12.460 --> 00:30:13.700
Show some mercy!

602
00:30:13.740 --> 00:30:14.670
Don't do it...

603
00:30:14.780 --> 00:30:17.320
These two fools are
dishonest to the core.

604
00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:18.760
They can't be trusted.

605
00:30:18.820 --> 00:30:19.820
Listen...

606
00:30:19.820 --> 00:30:20.320
I should mention that
our Log Pose was broken,

607
00:30:20.320 --> 00:30:23.930
and we don't have another one,
so still wanna ride with us?

608
00:30:24.260 --> 00:30:24.830
What...?! You broke it?!

609
00:30:25.580 --> 00:30:26.250
That was mine!

610
00:30:26.420 --> 00:30:27.580
Those aren't cheap, you know?!

611
00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:28.410
You're stuck here too?!

612
00:30:28.640 --> 00:30:29.980
How long were you
gonna make us beg

613
00:30:29.980 --> 00:30:31.520
before you bothered
to tell us?!

614
00:30:31.890 --> 00:30:33.310
Oh... Sorry... I forgot.

615
00:30:33.310 --> 00:30:36.480
Crocus gave us
his Log Pose, so...

616
00:30:37.320 --> 00:30:39.480
[MR. 9]
Oh! Please have pity on us!

617
00:30:39.860 --> 00:30:42.450
[MR. 9]
That lousy bitch!
She tricked us!

618
00:30:42.780 --> 00:30:44.280
It's fine...
You can ride with us.

619
00:30:45.700 --> 00:30:47.160
[LUFFY]
You said your home
is called Whisky Peak?

620
00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:48.330
Let's go there.

621
00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:51.160
Why?! These two are obviously
some pretty shady characters.

622
00:30:51.820 --> 00:30:53.290
Why would we
take them anywhere?!

623
00:30:54.710 --> 00:30:55.210
It's fine... Don't
sweat the small stuff.

624
00:30:55.740 --> 00:30:56.750
We'll be all right.

625
00:30:56.750 --> 00:30:58.180
Choose your route carefully.

626
00:30:58.180 --> 00:30:59.350
Once you head out from here,

627
00:30:59.350 --> 00:31:01.710
you'll be committed
to that course.

628
00:31:01.710 --> 00:31:02.620
That's okay.
If we don't like it,

629
00:31:02.650 --> 00:31:04.550
we'll try a different
route next time.

630
00:31:05.090 --> 00:31:06.470
I see...

631
00:31:07.010 --> 00:31:08.850
Okay...! It's time we get going!

632
00:31:10.220 --> 00:31:11.080
[LUFFY]
Now that me and
Laboon have an understanding,

633
00:31:11.540 --> 00:31:13.310
I can leave with
a clear conscience!

634
00:31:13.680 --> 00:31:16.060
Just who on earth do
you think you are anyway?

635
00:31:16.060 --> 00:31:17.900
What's that...? Me?

636
00:31:18.310 --> 00:31:20.480
Oh, I'm the man who'll
be King of the Pirates!

637
00:31:24.950 --> 00:31:26.530
[MISS WEDNESDAY]
Not too bright, this one...

638
00:31:29.410 --> 00:31:30.950
[CROCUS]
Should be good to go.

639
00:31:30.950 --> 00:31:33.000
The Log Pose has had plenty
of time to store the route.

640
00:31:33.620 --> 00:31:36.080
The needle should be pointing in
the same direction as the map.

641
00:31:37.540 --> 00:31:39.500
It's pointing
directly to Whisky Peak.

642
00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:41.840
[LUFFY]
See ya, pops!

643
00:31:41.840 --> 00:31:43.420
Thanks again for the
Log Pose! Take care!

644
00:31:43.460 --> 00:31:44.860
[CROCUS]
Have a safe trip, my boy!

645
00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:46.100
[LUFFY]
I'm off, Laboon!

646
00:31:46.100 --> 00:31:48.470
Be ready to fight
when I get back!

647
00:31:52.930 --> 00:31:54.890
[LUFFY]
Next stop, Whisky Peak!

648
00:31:54.890 --> 00:31:57.270
Ready gang...?!
Let's set sail...

649
00:32:16.350 --> 00:32:17.180
I wonder...

650
00:32:17.220 --> 00:32:19.750
Luffy and his
exuberant crew could be

651
00:32:19.990 --> 00:32:21.790
the very pirates
we've been waiting for...

652
00:32:22.330 --> 00:32:25.130
That young captain
sure has a way about him.

653
00:32:25.460 --> 00:32:27.930
It's uncanny really...

654
00:32:28.800 --> 00:32:31.720
[CROCUS]
Wouldn't you agree... Roger?

